     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br>On Friday, September 16, 2016 at 10:46:37 AM UTC-4, Xiaoyang Feng wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Guys,<div><br></div><div>I am new to shiny and I tried to search before post. I did not find the answer I need, maybe I searched wrong keywords. </div><div><br></div><div>Here is my problem. I made a nav page for navigation of all the shiny apps my co-works made. See the code below. </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> navbarMenu</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">title </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Production&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                           tabPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;BreedingInventory&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                                    HTML</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;&lt;iframe src=&quot;app1url&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot; seamless height=&quot;1000px&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                           </span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                           tabPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;BreedTarget&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                                    HTML</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;&lt;iframe src=&quot;app2url&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot; seamless height=&quot;1000px&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                           </span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>So, when I run my shiny app, it rendering every tabPanel in the background. It really slow(I have around 40 tabPanels, going to be more). Is there a way to render only active tabPanel? </div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
